.policy "fastapi-practice-yield-dependency-cleanup" revision 1
.description "Release a FastAPI yield dependency's resources in a finally block around the yield, and re-raise in its except handlers, so a failing request neither leaks a connection nor loses its error."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*.py"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. FastAPI (since 0.110, and as plain generator semantics have it) throws the route's
// exception into a dependency that yields, at its `yield`. Code after the `yield` that no `finally` (or `with`)
// covers then never runs, so every failing request leaks what that code would have released; repeated errors
// exhaust the pool ("QueuePool limit of size 5 overflow 10 reached"). An `except` around the `yield` that does not
// re-raise hides the error: FastAPI (0.124 and later) answers 500 and logs only "Response not awaited ... not raising
// the exception again", so the route's own exception and traceback are lost and an HTTPException(404) becomes a 500.
// The rule reads generators that lib/fastapi's fa_yield_dep calls dependencies (some `Depends(...)` of the run names
// them, in any module: the generator in db.py, the `Depends` in deps.py or a route; a class's `__call__` through
// `Depends(instance)` or a name bound to the instance), outside test code, and reports in the generator's own frame:
//   - UnprotectedCleanup: a call to `close`, `aclose`, `release`, `remove`, `dispose`, `shutdown`, `disconnect`,
//     `terminate`, `cleanup`, `unlink` or `rollback` (awaited or not) after the `yield`, unless the `yield` sits in a
//     `with`/`async with` block, the call is in the `finally` of a `try` whose body holds the `yield`, the call is in
//     an `except` handler (it runs on the error path; SwallowedError judges the handler), or the call is in the body
//     of a `try` around the `yield` whose `finally` or `except` also releases something.
//   - SwallowedError: an `except` clause of a `try` whose body holds the `yield`, catching `Exception`,
//     `BaseException`, everything (bare `except:`), or a database or HTTP error class (`SQLAlchemyError`,
//     `DBAPIError`, `DatabaseError`, `OperationalError`, `IntegrityError`, `HTTPException`, or anything from
//     `sqlalchemy.exc`), alone or in a tuple, whose handler can finish without raising: its last statement is not a
//     `raise`, or is an `if` without `else` or with a branch that can finish (lib/django's py_reraising_handler), or
//     is a call of a def of the run whose every path ends in `raise` or that is annotated `-> NoReturn`/`-> Never`
//     (`abort(500)`).
//   db.py:    def get_db(): db = SessionLocal(); yield db; db.close()              reported at db.close()
//   db.py:    try: yield db  except Exception: db.rollback()                      reported at the except
//   deps.py:  SessionDep = Annotated[Session, Depends(get_db)]                     makes get_db a dependency;
//             `rw = Depends(write_session)` with `write_session = WriteSession()` makes `WriteSession.__call__` one
// Left alone: `try: yield db finally: db.close()`; `with SessionLocal() as db: yield db` and `async with`; `try: yield
// db; db.commit() except: db.rollback(); raise finally: db.close()`; `commit()` after the yield (an error skips it on
// purpose; moving it into `finally` would commit failed requests); handlers that re-raise or raise a new exception on
// every path; handlers for other classes (`except KeyboardInterrupt`); statements after the yield that release
// nothing (logging, metrics); generators no `Depends` names (`@contextmanager` helpers, pytest fixtures); test files.
// A release written after a `try` around the yield whose handler re-raises is reported: the raise skips it
// (python-practice-contextmanager-cleanup-skipped, for `@contextmanager` generators, leaves that shape alone).
// Gaps: cleanup in a helper the generator calls after the yield (`_release(db)`) is not seen; a `with` around the
// yield silences every call after it, even one on another resource; a raising helper is followed one call deep; a
// handler for a project's own class (`except AppError: pass`) is not reported.

#include "lib/fastapi.rerail"

// Whether a generator is a dependency is a question over the run's files (the `Depends` may sit in any module): the
// rules below read every generator of a file at its nodes, and the outputs ask lib/fastapi's fa_dependency by the
// generator's symbol (pt_def).
.violation UnprotectedCleanup(at: node, what: symbol, fx: symbol)
    "`{what}` after the `yield` in dependency `{fx}` is skipped when the route raises, leaking what it releases; move it into `finally:` around the `yield`, or use `with ... as x: yield x`."
UnprotectedCleanup(c, what, fx) :- yd_cleanup(c, g, _), yd_yield(g, y), earlier(y, c), !yd_protected(c, y),
    def_name(g, fx), field(c, "function", fn), text(fn, ft), what = cat(ft, "()"), pt_def(g, gq), fa_dependency(gq).
.violation SwallowedError(at: node, fx: symbol)
    "This `except` around the `yield` in dependency `{fx}` can finish without raising, so the route's own error and traceback are lost and an HTTPException turns into a 500; end the handler with `raise`."
SwallowedError(x, fx) :- yd_swallow(x, g), yd_handler(x, hb), yd_may_end(hb), def_name(g, fx), pt_def(g, gq),
    fa_dependency(gq).
SwallowedError(x, fx) :- yd_swallow(x, g), yd_handler(x, hb), yd_end_tail(hb, s), yd_place(s, p, t),
    !yd_raising_at(p, t), def_name(g, fx), pt_def(g, gq), fa_dependency(gq).
// yd_swallow(x, g): except clause x, of a try whose body holds a yield of generator g, catches the route's errors.
.decl yd_swallow(x: node, g: node)
yd_swallow(x, g) :- yd_yield(g, y), yd_try_around(t, y), child(t, x, _), kind(x, "except_clause"), yd_catches(x).

// ---- dependencies ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// yd_dep(g): a generator outside test code (a dependency when fa_dependency names it). yd_yield(g, y): a yield in its
// own frame.
.decl yd_dep(g: node)
yd_dep(g) :- kind(g, "function_definition"), kind(y, "yield"), def_frame(y, g), docof(g, d), !fa_test_doc(d).
.decl yd_yield(g: node, y: node)
yd_yield(g, y) :- yd_dep(g), kind(y, "yield"), def_frame(y, g).

// ---- cleanup -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// yd_release(m): methods that release or reset a resource. `commit` is not one: skipping it on an error is right.
.decl yd_release(m: symbol)
yd_release("close"). yd_release("aclose"). yd_release("release"). yd_release("remove"). yd_release("dispose").
yd_release("shutdown"). yd_release("disconnect"). yd_release("terminate"). yd_release("cleanup").
yd_release("unlink"). yd_release("rollback").
// yd_cleanup(c, g, m): call c of method or function m releases something, in dependency g's own frame.
.decl yd_cleanup(c: node, g: node, m: symbol)
yd_cleanup(c, g, m) :- yd_dep(g), kind(c, "call"), def_frame(c, g), call_name(c, m), yd_release(m).
// yd_try_around(t, y): y is in the body of try statement t (not its handlers, else or finally).
.decl yd_try_around(t: node, y: node)
yd_try_around(t, y) :- yd_yield(_, y), kind(t, "try_statement"), field(t, "body", b), within(y, b).
// yd_releases(k): clause k (a finally or an except) holds a release, or a commit.
.decl yd_releases(k: node)
yd_releases(k) :- (kind(k, "finally_clause") ; kind(k, "except_clause")), within(c, k), kind(c, "call"),
    call_name(c, m), (yd_release(m) ; m = "commit").
// yd_protected(c, y): the error thrown in at y still reaches cleanup c, or a context manager does the cleanup.
.decl yd_protected(c: node, y: node)
yd_protected(c, y) :- yd_cleanup(c, g, _), yd_yield(g, y), kind(w, "with_statement"), def_frame(w, g), within(y, w).
yd_protected(c, y) :- yd_cleanup(c, g, _), yd_yield(g, y), kind(x, "except_clause"), def_frame(x, g), within(c, x).
yd_protected(c, y) :- yd_cleanup(c, _, _), yd_try_around(t, y), child(t, k, _), kind(k, "finally_clause"),
    within(c, k).
yd_protected(c, y) :- yd_cleanup(c, _, _), yd_try_around(t, y), field(t, "body", b), within(c, b), child(t, k, _),
    yd_releases(k).

// ---- handlers ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// yd_exc_val(x, t): the class expression except clause x names, `as e` and parentheses off.
.decl yd_exc_val(x: node, t: node)
yd_exc_val(x, v) :- kind(x, "except_clause"), field(x, "value", v0), unparen(v0, v), !kind(v, "as_pattern").
yd_exc_val(x, t) :- kind(x, "except_clause"), field(x, "value", v0), unparen(v0, v), kind(v, "as_pattern"),
    child(v, t0, 0), unparen(t0, t).
// yd_exc_type(x, e): x handles class expression e: `except (A, B)` gives A and B.
.decl yd_exc_type(x: node, e: node)
yd_exc_type(x, e) :- yd_exc_val(x, t), kind(t, "tuple"), child(t, e0, _), !kind(e0, "comment"), unparen(e0, e).
yd_exc_type(x, t) :- yd_exc_val(x, t), !kind(t, "tuple").
// yd_broad_name(x): classes whose handler around a dependency's yield catches the route's errors.
.decl yd_broad_name(x: symbol)
yd_broad_name("Exception"). yd_broad_name("BaseException"). yd_broad_name("SQLAlchemyError").
yd_broad_name("DBAPIError"). yd_broad_name("DatabaseError"). yd_broad_name("OperationalError").
yd_broad_name("IntegrityError"). yd_broad_name("HTTPException").
// yd_catches(x): x is a bare `except:`, or names such a class (by its last name, or anything from sqlalchemy.exc).
.decl yd_catches(x: node)
yd_catches(x) :- kind(x, "except_clause"), !field(x, "value", _).
yd_catches(x) :- yd_exc_type(x, e), leaf_name(e, n), yd_broad_name(n).
yd_catches(x) :- yd_exc_type(x, e), sym_of(e, q), prefix("sqlalchemy.exc.", q).

// yd_handler(x, hb): hb is except clause x's handler block.
.decl yd_handler(x: node, hb: node)
yd_handler(x, hb) :- kind(x, "except_clause"), child(x, hb, _), kind(hb, "block").
// A handler can finish without raising when a path through it (lib/django's py_reraising_handler, copied) does not
// end in `raise`. A path is followed through the handler's last statement: a `raise`, or an if/elif/else (with an
// else) all of whose branches end so; a raise inside a nested try, with or match counts as not raising.
// yd_may_end(b): a path of block b ends in a statement that is no raise and no call of a def of the run, or in an if
// with no else. yd_end_tail(b, s): a path of b ends in statement s, a call of a def of the run (yd_end_call), which
// ends the path only when that def can return: the def may be in another file, so the outputs ask yd_raising_at, by
// the statement's place.
.decl yd_raise_block(b: node)
yd_raise_block(b) :- yd_handler(_, b).
yd_raise_block(b) :- yd_raise_block(p), body_len(p, k), j = k - 1, body_stmt(p, s, j), kind(s, "if_statement"),
    yd_if_branch(s, b).
.decl yd_if_branch(s: node, b: node)
yd_if_branch(s, b) :- kind(s, "if_statement"), field(s, "consequence", b).
yd_if_branch(s, b) :- kind(s, "if_statement"), field(s, "alternative", e), kind(e, "elif_clause"),
    field(e, "consequence", b).
yd_if_branch(s, b) :- kind(s, "if_statement"), field(s, "alternative", e), kind(e, "else_clause"), field(e, "body", b).
.decl yd_has_else(s: node)
yd_has_else(s) :- kind(s, "if_statement"), field(s, "alternative", e), kind(e, "else_clause").
.decl yd_may_end(b: node)
yd_may_end(b) :- yd_raise_block(b), body_len(b, k), j = k - 1, body_stmt(b, s, j), !kind(s, "raise_statement"),
    !kind(s, "if_statement"), !yd_end_call(s, _).
yd_may_end(b) :- yd_raise_block(b), body_len(b, k), j = k - 1, body_stmt(b, s, j), kind(s, "if_statement"),
    !yd_has_else(s).
yd_may_end(b) :- yd_raise_block(b), body_len(b, k), j = k - 1, body_stmt(b, s, j), yd_if_branch(s, cb), yd_may_end(cb).
.decl yd_end_tail(b: node, s: node)
yd_end_tail(b, s) :- yd_raise_block(b), body_len(b, k), j = k - 1, body_stmt(b, s, j), yd_end_call(s, _).
yd_end_tail(b, s) :- yd_raise_block(b), body_len(b, k), j = k - 1, body_stmt(b, s2, j), yd_if_branch(s2, cb),
    yd_end_tail(cb, s).

// A handler that ends in a call of a helper that always raises (`abort(500)`), one call deep: the helper's body is
// read with the same path rule, without following its own calls.
// yd_end_call(s, h): statement s, the last of a handler's path, calls def h of the run (its symbol: python/calls'
// call_target). yd_place(s, p, t): its path and term (python/points-to-file's pt_tm); yd_tail_at(p, t, h): the call
// by those symbols.
.decl yd_end_call(s: node, h: symbol)
yd_end_call(s, h) :- yd_raise_block(b), body_len(b, k), j = k - 1, body_stmt(b, s, j),
    kind(s, "expression_statement"), child(s, c0, 0), unparen(c0, c), kind(c, "call"), call_target(c, h).
.decl yd_place(s: node, p: symbol, t: symbol)
yd_place(s, p, t) :- yd_end_call(s, _), docof(s, d), doc(d, p, _), pt_tm(s, t).
.decl yd_tail_at(p: symbol, t: symbol, h: symbol)
yd_tail_at(p, t, h) :- yd_end_call(s, h), yd_place(s, p, t).
// The helper may be in any file, so every def is read: yd_hblock(b) is a block of a def's body path.
.decl yd_hblock(b: node)
yd_hblock(b) :- kind(h, "function_definition"), field(h, "body", b).
yd_hblock(b) :- yd_hblock(p), body_len(p, k), j = k - 1, body_stmt(p, s, j), kind(s, "if_statement"), yd_if_branch(s, b).
.decl yd_hmay_end(b: node)
yd_hmay_end(b) :- yd_hblock(b), body_len(b, k), j = k - 1, body_stmt(b, s, j), !kind(s, "raise_statement"),
    !kind(s, "if_statement").
yd_hmay_end(b) :- yd_hblock(b), body_len(b, k), j = k - 1, body_stmt(b, s, j), kind(s, "if_statement"),
    !yd_has_else(s).
yd_hmay_end(b) :- yd_hblock(b), body_len(b, k), j = k - 1, body_stmt(b, s, j), yd_if_branch(s, cb), yd_hmay_end(cb).
// yd_noreturn(h): every path of def h ends in `raise`, or h is annotated `-> NoReturn` / `-> Never`; by its symbol,
// stated in its file.
.decl yd_noreturn_def(h: node)
yd_noreturn_def(h) :- kind(h, "function_definition"), field(h, "body", b), !yd_hmay_end(b).
yd_noreturn_def(h) :- kind(h, "function_definition"), field(h, "return_type", t0), fa_strip(t0, t),
    (leaf_name(t, "NoReturn") ; leaf_name(t, "Never")).
.decl yd_noreturn(h: symbol)
yd_noreturn(hq) :- yd_noreturn_def(h), pt_def(h, hq).
// yd_raising_at(p, t): the handler's last call at (p, t) calls a def that never returns.
.decl yd_raising_at(p: symbol, t: symbol)
yd_raising_at(p, t) :- yd_tail_at(p, t, h), yd_noreturn(h).

// The cases, `cases/fastapi-practice-yield-dependency-cleanup/`, read as one repository: each line ending in
// `# caught` is reported, and no other line.
.test cases exactly
    .fixture "app/__init__.py" from "../cases/fastapi-practice-yield-dependency-cleanup/app/__init__.py"
    .fixture "app/db.py" from "../cases/fastapi-practice-yield-dependency-cleanup/app/db.py"
    .fixture "app/deps.py" from "../cases/fastapi-practice-yield-dependency-cleanup/app/deps.py"
    .fixture "app/fixtures.py" from "../cases/fastapi-practice-yield-dependency-cleanup/app/fixtures.py"
    .fixture "app/routes.py" from "../cases/fastapi-practice-yield-dependency-cleanup/app/routes.py"
    .fixture "app/tests/__init__.py" from "../cases/fastapi-practice-yield-dependency-cleanup/app/tests/__init__.py"
    .fixture "app/tests/test_routes.py" from "../cases/fastapi-practice-yield-dependency-cleanup/app/tests/test_routes.py"
    .expect _ at "app/db.py":29
    .expect _ at "app/db.py":36
    .expect _ at "app/db.py":44
    .expect _ at "app/db.py":55
    .expect _ at "app/db.py":63
    .expect _ at "app/db.py":76
    .expect _ at "app/db.py":86
    .expect _ at "app/db.py":94
    .expect _ at "app/db.py":105
    .expect _ at "app/db.py":116
    .expect _ at "app/db.py":125
    .expect _ at "app/db.py":136
    .expect _ at "app/db.py":288
    .expect _ at "app/routes.py":18
    .expect _ at "app/routes.py":26
.end
